      "text": "Deer Lodge began as a health resort in the 1880s, founded by former Rugby colonist Abner Ross.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Lodge%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ross built the Victorian‑style Walnut Knoll house, sparking a wave of similarly styled homes in the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Lodge%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the 1890s, Deer Lodge boasted two hotels, a newspaper, a theater, and a planing mill, making it a bustling resort town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Lodge%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Deer Lodge Historical Society, located at 302 Old Deer Lodge Pike, preserves local artifacts and hosts educational events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
